   "title": {
    "zh": "关键路径的代价",
    "en": "The Cost of the Critical Path"
   },
   "why": {
    "zh": "一道菜经过几位厨师，每人一分钟，端去另一间厨房要多走三分钟：快慢看最长的那条路跨了几次院子。十二道工序的大菜逐个得到“最早几分钟”；两间厨房都要 g 和 j，就各做一份；从成品往回推，开出八间厨房、二十个人；不许做两份时，最快只有 10。",
    "en": "A dish passes through cooks a minute each, and carrying it to another kitchen costs three more: speed depends on how often the longest route crosses the yard. A twelve-step banquet gets its earliest minutes one by one; two kitchens both need g and j, so each makes its own; working back from the dishes opens eight kitchens with twenty cooks; without copies the best is 10."
   },
